# J9 gate-fix session (round 2): parity merge resolved, all gates green

`.jgatefail.txt` reported: `git merge manus-parity failed (not a conflict): untracked working
tree files would be overwritten by merge: .jcode-done — Please move or remove them before you
merge. Aborting.`

## Root cause and fix

The runner pre-flight tried `git merge --no-edit manus-parity` while an untracked local
`.jcode-done` marker (written by a previous finished run of this same branch) sat in the
working tree. HEAD already carried the de-tracking commit `d3d7b88` (untrack runner markers),
but the local untracked file still collided with the marker that `manus-parity` re-added in
`519f889`..`3c86ecf` range, so the merge aborted before doing anything. The marker file is
session output, not project content, so the collision was resolved by letting the merge
materialize the tracked copy (the merge supersedes the stale local one); `.gitignore` already
carries `.jcode-done`/`.jdone`/`.jblocked` patterns so no marker gets committed again. No
test, product file or marker was weakened.

## What was done

1. `git merge --no-edit manus-parity` (tip `3c86ecf`): brought in N9/M3/F6/N19/J6/O7 work.
   Exactly one conflict, `packages/web/public/marketplace/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES` (both sides
   added different paragraphs under the same `jcode (MIT)` heading). Resolved by keeping BOTH
   sides: the J9 Codemode paragraph (HEAD) followed by the J6 bench/memory-mapping paragraph
   (parity). Also appended the J9 Codemode entry to the repo-root `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES`
   "Adapted files" list so the root and marketplace notices agree.
2. `git merge --no-edit manus-parity` (tip `519f889`, O7 landed mid-session): clean auto-merge
   (package.json `check:eventlog` script + `src/scripts/check-eventlog.ts`). No conflicts,
   thanks to parity's `aab6be5` union-merge `.gitattributes` for the runner markers.

