- `npm run build:server`                      -> exit 0 (dist/server.cjs ~21.6 MB)
- `(cd packages/web && npx next build)`       -> exit 0 (25/25 static pages)
- `npm run verify`                            -> exit 0 (typecheck, encoding, eval, orchestrator, recovery, modes)
- `npm run check:eventlog`                    -> PASS (all four O7 checks)
- `node --import tsx --test "src/codemode/__tests__/*.test.ts"` -> 46/46 pass
- `node --import tsx --test src/server/__tests__/runTools.test.ts src/server/__tests__/dataControls.test.ts` -> 21/21 pass
- `(cd packages/web && npx vitest run src/components/settings)` -> 12 files / 50 tests pass
- `node --import tsx --test "src/**/*.test.ts"` -> **2988 tests / 2988 pass / 0 fail**

## J9 acceptance re-verified on the merged tree

- The read+grep 20x fan-out test passes with transcript growth asserted < 2 KB
  (`src/codemode/__tests__/tool.test.ts`).
- No-fs/net/process, timeout, memory limit and policy-denied-tool tests all pass
  (46 codemode tests, 0 fail).
- Bundling: the singlefile QuickJS variant's wasm is inlined into `dist/server.cjs`
  (raw `\0asm` header bytes present as an escaped template literal at offset ~15.47 MB).
  A throwaway esbuild probe (same bundling as build:server, then deleted) imported
  `src/codemode/wasmLoader.ts`, bundled to CJS, and evaluated `2 + 3` inside the sandbox
  from the bundle: QUICKJS_BUNDLED_VALUE 5. So the sandbox boots from esbuild output.

No secrets committed. No forbidden path touched. No test weakened, deleted or skipped.
No Arabic text was written; no mojibake placeholder text was added.
